<title>FRANCE: Thomson-CSF, Hughes to bid for NATO deal.</title>
<headline>Thomson-CSF, Hughes to bid for NATO deal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thomson-CSF's Airsys unit and Hughes Aircraft said they set up a new company to bid for NATO's tender for an Air Command and Control System (ACCS).</p>
<p>The ACCS programme is to replace NATO's existing air defence system NADGE, the companies said.</p>
<p>Hughes Aircraft is a unit of Hughes Electronics, a subsidiary of General Motors.</p>
<p>The new company will be owned in equal proportions by Airsys and Hughes Aircraft and be called Air Command Systems International and will be governed by French law.</p>
<p>The new company will pursue the new programme with European companies Alenia, a unit of Finmeccanica, Dasa-Dornier, Siemens-Plessey and GEC-Marconi.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
